\title{Bet-time cutoff: as-of feature joins}
\description{
Wraps existing rolling-feature outputs with a bet-time cutoff so
that a match M at date \code{t_M} sees only feature values whose source
data is observed at dates \verb{<= t_M - cutoff_days}. This defends
against the Wednesday-for-Monday leakage pattern, where a feature
for a Saturday match is contaminated by a midweek fixture played
between Pinnacle's opening price and kickoff.
}
\details{
The existing \code{rolling_goals()} and \code{compute_elo()} already produce
"pre-match" time series (one row per team per match date with the
state \emph{just before} that match). Applying an as-of join that looks
up the latest such row with \code{feature_date <= target_date - cutoff}
gives a strictly leak-free feature value without touching their
internals.

Freshness trade-off: the cutoff feature is what the bettor would
have seen \code{cutoff_days} before kickoff, not what the latest row
immediately before the bet timestamp would have been. For a team
whose most recent match was \code{d} days ago, the cutoff feature is
equivalent to the standard feature if \code{d >= cutoff_days}, and
slightly staler if \code{d < cutoff_days} (in which case it reflects an
earlier row).
}
